@model CBS.FrontDesk.Data.Entity.MemberOperation.MemberOperationPanel


<div class="card mb-1">
    <h6 class="card-header d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center text-primary">
        <span><i class="mdi mdi-information-outline me-2"></i> Loan Application Tips</span>
        <button class="btn btn-light btn-sm" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseLoanTips" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseLoanTips">
            <i class="mdi mdi-chevron-down"></i>
        </button>
    </h6>
    <div id="collapseLoanTips" class="collapse">
        <div class="card-body">
            <p class="text-muted mb-2">Follow these tips to ensure a successful loan application process:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Ensure all loan details, including loan type, term, and repayment cycle, are accurately selected.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Validate the member's eligibility before proceeding. Check if the member meets the minimum shares and savings requirements.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Use the "Override Balance" section responsibly during loan refinancing or rescheduling and ensure proper documentation is provided.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Verify the co-obligor's account balance if the loan requires a co-obligor. Co-obligor accounts must have sufficient balances to assure the loan.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-warning me-2"></i> Ensure that all blocked accounts used as guarantees are compliant with loan policies.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Risk mitigation measures, such as collateral and guarantors, should be accurately detailed in the application.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Ensure all required documents for loan approval are uploaded to avoid rejection.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Validate that all fees, including processing and inspection fees, are clearly defined and approved by the Loan Manager.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-muted">Additional Notes:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Trust will not grant a loan if the member does not meet the requirements set by the Loan Management Board. These requirements include:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Minimum Shares: e.g., 75,000</li>
                        <li>Minimum Savings: e.g., 20% of the loan amount</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> If a down payment is required, it must be fulfilled as per the board's criteria. Down payment typically covers:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Savings account</li>
                        <li>Ordinary shares</li>
                        <li>Deposit account</li>
                        <li>Salary account</li>
                    </ul>
                    Default loan requirements: 20% from savings and 75,000 in shares.
                </li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Co-obligors must be provided for Special Saving Facility (SSF) loans. The co-obligor must have sufficient balance to assure the loan.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Accounts used as guarantees are blocked until the loan is fully settled.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-0">
    <h6 class="card-header d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center text-danger">
        <span><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline me-2"></i> Important Notices</span>
        <button class="btn btn-light btn-sm" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseNotices" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseNotices">
            <i class="mdi mdi-chevron-down"></i>
        </button>
    </h6>
    <div id="collapseNotices" class="collapse">
        <div class="card-body">
            <ul>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> The "Override Balance" section should only be used when refinancing or rescheduling a loan, with proper documentation and approval.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Any changes to loan balances, interest rates, or penalties must be supported by valid evidence and authorized by the Loan Manager.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Any change in balance information will override the existing balance information. Proceed with caution and ensure values are accurate before saving.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> VAT is calculated automatically based on the interest inputted. Ensure the interest rate is accurate to avoid discrepancies.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Changes made to balance information cannot be undone. Verify all inputs before finalizing the application.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Every loan process requires supporting documentation. Ensure all necessary documents are uploaded before submitting the loan application.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Ensure all mandatory fields, including loan amount, repayment schedule, and risk mitigation measures, are accurately completed to avoid delays.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> For loans requiring upfront fees, ensure the fees are paid before processing or disbursement to prevent rejection.</li>
                <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i> Loan approval and processing are subject to verification of borrower credentials and compliance with regulatory requirements.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>



@using (Html.BeginForm("Create", "MemberOperation", FormMethod.Post, new { enctype = "multipart/form-data", onsubmit = "return AjaxPostAndUpdate(this);" }))
{
    @Html.HiddenFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.CustomerId)
    <input type="hidden" value="@Model.AddLoanApplicationCommand.CustomerId" id="customerid" />
    <br />
    <div class="row">
        <div class="accordion" id="collapsibleSection">
            <div class="card accordion-item mb-3">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingDeliveryAddress">
                    <button type="button"
                            class="accordion-button"
                            data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                            data-bs-target="#collapseDeliveryAddress"
                            aria-expanded="true"
                            aria-controls="collapseDeliveryAddress">
                        Loan product
                        <i class="mdi mdi-help-circle text-primary ms-2" data-bs-toggle="tooltip" title="Loan Product: This section allows you to select the appropriate loan product for the loan application. Here's a breakdown of the key components:
Key Points:
1. Select Loan Product Dropdown: Use this dropdown menu to choose the specific loan product that best fits the borrower's needs. The available options are populated based on the loan products available in the system.
2. Select Loan Type Dropdown: This dropdown menu enables you to specify the type of loan being applied for. It could be a personal loan, business loan, mortgage, etc.
3. Amount: Enter the desired loan amount in this field.
4. Loan Duration: Specify the intended duration of the loan in months or years.
5. Help Icon: Click on the help icon (ℹ️) next to the &quot;Loan Product&quot; heading for additional assistance and guidance on selecting the most suitable loan product for the borrower's needs.
By carefully selecting the appropriate loan product and terms in this section, you can ensure that the loan meets the borrower's needs while also aligning with their financial capabilities and objectives."></i>
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapseDeliveryAddress"
                     class="accordion-collapse collapse show"
                     data-bs-parent="#collapsibleSection">
                    <br />
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <fieldset class="fieldset-custom">
                            <div class="row g-4">
                                <div class="col-md-12">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.DropDownListFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanApplicationType, new SelectList(ViewBag.LoanApplicationTypes, "Value", "Text"), "---Select loan application types---", new { @class = "form-control select2", @search = "true", @id = "LoanApplicationType", @onchange = "LoadRefinancing(this.value,'loanapplicationtype','loanid')" })
                                        <label>Application type</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-md-12">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.DropDownListFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanProductCategoryId, new SelectList(ViewBag.Categories, "Id", "Name"), "---Select loan product category---", new { @class = "form-control select2", @search = "true", @id = "LoanCategoryId", @onchange = "GetLoanPurposes(this.value,'purposeId')" })
                                        <label>Select loan product category</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-md-12">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.DropDownListFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanTermId, new SelectList(ViewBag.LoanTerms, "Id", "Name"), "---Select loan term---", new { @class = "form-control select2", @search = "true", @id = "LoanTermId", @onchange = "GetConfiuredTargets(this.value,'TargetId')" })
                                        <label>Select loan term</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-12" id="LoanCategoryDive">
                                    <div class="form-check form-check-inline" id="accountType">
                                        @Html.RadioButtonFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanCategory, "Main_Loan", new { id = "MainLoan", @class = "form-check-input" })
                                        <label class="form-check-label" for="MainLoan">Main Loan</label>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="form-check form-check-inline">
                                        @Html.RadioButtonFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanCategory, "Special_Saving_Facility_Loan", new { id = "SpecialSavingFacilityLoan", @class = "form-check-input" })
                                        <label class="form-check-label" for="SpecialSavingFacilityLoan">Special Saving Facility</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-md-12" id="TargetPopulationDiv">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.DropDownListFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanTarget, new SelectList(ViewBag.LoanTargets, "Value", "Text"), "---Select loan category---", new { @class = "form-control select2", @search = "true", @onchange = "GetProductByTarget(this.value,'loan_productid')", @id = "TargetId" })
                                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanTarget, "", new { @class = "text-danger " })
                                        <label>Targeted population</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <!-- Adjusted row -->
                                <div id="loandiv" style="display:none;">
                                    <h5 id="repaymentHeader">Select loan to refinance</h5>
                                    <div class="card mb-4">
                                        <h6 class="card-header d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center text-primary">
                                            <span><i class="mdi mdi-information-outline me-2"></i> TIPS</span>
                                            <button class="btn btn-light btn-sm" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseHelpTips" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseHelpTips">
                                                <i class="mdi mdi-chevron-down"></i>
                                            </button>
                                        </h6>
                                        <div id="collapseHelpTips" class="collapse">
                                            <div class="card-body">
                                                <p class="text-muted mb-2">Follow these tips to ensure a smooth refinancing process:</p>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Select the loan to refinance from the dropdown. Ensure the member's loan list is up-to-date.</li>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Use the "Override Balance" section only if necessary, and verify amounts before proceeding.</li>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Enable "Stop further interest calculations" only when the loan has been fully settled or adjusted.</li>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-check-circle-outline text-success me-2"></i> Fill out the repayment details accurately to avoid mismatches in the system.</li>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-warning me-2"></i> Any changes in the loan balance, interest, VAT, or penalties must be justified with proper documentation.</li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <p class="text-muted">Additional Notes:</p>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-information-outline text-primary me-2"></i> Ensure all repayment details, including capital, interest, and penalty amounts, match the agreement.</li>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-information-outline text-primary me-2"></i> Verify the loan reference before finalizing the refinancing process.</li>
                                                    <li><i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-warning me-2"></i> For any discrepancies, consult the Loan Manager before submission.</li>
                                                </ul>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="col-md-12 mb-4">
                                        <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                            @Html.DropDownListFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanId, new SelectList(ViewBag.MembersLoan, "Value", "Text"), "---Select loan---", new { @class = "form-control select2", @search = "true", @id = "loanid", @onchange = "GetLoan(this.value)" })
                                            @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanId, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                            <label>Member current loans</label>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>

                                    <!-- Balance, Interest, VAT, Penalty inputs -->
                                    <div class="col-md-12 mb-4">
                                        <div class="form-check">
                                            @Html.CheckBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.IsOverRightOldLoanInterestAndBalance, new { @class = "form-check-input", @id = "IsOverRightOldLoanInterestAndBalance" })
                                            <label class="form-check-label" for="IsOverRightOldLoanInterestAndBalance">Override loan balance & Process Repayment</label>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>

                                    <div class="row" id="loanoveride" style="display:none;">
                                        <div style="display:none">
                                            <div class="col-md-3">
                                                <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                    @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewBalance, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "NewBalance" })
                                                    @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewBalance, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                    <label for="NewBalance">Override Balance</label>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="col-md-3">
                                                <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                    @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewInterest, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "NewInterest" })
                                                    @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewInterest, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                    <label for="NewInterest">Override Interest</label>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="col-md-3">
                                                <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                    @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewVAT, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "NewVAT" })
                                                    @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewVAT, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                    <label for="NewVAT">Override VAT</label>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="col-md-3 mb-3">
                                                <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                    @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewPenalty, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "NewPenalty" })
                                                    @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.NewPenalty, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                    <label for="NewPenalty">Override Penalty</label>
                                                </div>
                                            </div>

                                        </div>
                                        <div class="col-md-12 mb-4">
                                            <div class="form-check">
                                                @Html.CheckBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.StopInterestCalculation, new { @class = "form-check-input", @id = "StopInterestCalculation" })
                                                <label class="form-check-label" for="StopInterestCalculation">Stop further interest calculations.</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <!-- Repayment Details -->
                                        <h5>Repayment Details</h5>
                                        <div class="col-md-3 mb-3">
                                            <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Capital, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "oldLoanCapital", @onchange = "calculateVATAndTotal()" })
                                                @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Capital, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                <label for="oldLoanCapital">Capital</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="col-md-3 mb-3">
                                            <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Interest, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "oldLoanInterest", @onchange = "calculateVATAndTotal()" })
                                                @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Interest, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                <label for="oldLoanInterest">Interest</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="col-md-2 mb-2">
                                            <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.VatRate, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "oldLoanvatRate", @readonly = "readonly" })
                                                <label for="oldLoanvatRate">V.Rate</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="col-md-2 mb-2">
                                            <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.VAT, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "oldLoanVAT", @readonly = "readonly" })
                                                @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.VAT, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                <label for="oldLoanVAT">VAT</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="col-md-2 mb-3">
                                            <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Amount, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "oldLoanAmount", @readonly = "readonly" })
                                                @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Amount, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                <label for="oldLoanAmount">D.Amount</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>

                                        <div class="col-md-3 mb-3">
                                            <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Penalty, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "oldLoanPenalty", @onchange = "calculateVATAndTotal()" })
                                                @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.Penalty, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                <label for="oldLoanPenalty">Penalty</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="col-md-9 mb-3">
                                            <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                                @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.LoanId, new { @class = "form-control", @id = "oldLoanLoanId", @readonly = "readonly" })
                                                @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.OldLoanPayment.LoanId, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                                <label for="oldLoanLoanId">Loan Reference</label>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-md-12" id="loanProductDiv">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.DropDownListFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanProductId, new SelectList(ViewBag.LoanProducts, "Value", "Text"), "---Select loan product---", new { @class = "form-control select2", @search = "true", @onchange = "LoanProductsProperties(this.value,'loanrepayment_cycles','RepaymentCircle')", @id = "loan_productid" })
                                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanProductId, "", new { @class = "text-danger " })
                                        <label>Loan product</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-md-12" id="loanTypeDiv">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.DropDownListFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanType, new SelectList(ViewBag.LoanTypes, "Value", "Text"), "---Select loan type---", new { @class = "form-control select2", @search = "true" })
                                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanType, "", new { @class = "text-danger " })
                                        <label>Select loan type</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="col-md-12" id="RAmountDiv">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.Amount, new { @class = "form-control" })
                                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.Amount, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                        <label id="amount">Amount</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-md-12">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
                                        @Html.TextBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanDuration, new { @class = "form-control" })
                                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.LoanDuration, "", new { @class = "text-danger" })
                                        <label id="loanduration">Loan duration</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-12" id="beforeProcessingDiv">
                                    <div class="form-check">
                                        @Html.CheckBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.IsPaidFeeBeforeProcessing, new { @class = "form-check-input", @id = "FeePaidBeforeProcessing" })
                                        <label class="form-check-label" for="FeePaidBeforeProcessing">
                                            A partial fee must be paid before the loan can be processed at the cash desk, depending on the loan product configuration.
                                        </label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-12" id="afterProcessingDiv">
                                    <div class="form-check">
                                        @Html.CheckBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.IsPaidFeeAfterProcessing, new { @class = "form-check-input", @id = "FeePaidAfterProcessing" })
                                        <label class="form-check-label" for="FeePaidAfterProcessing">
                                            The fee can either be paid upfront at the cash desk before disbursement, or deducted directly from the loan after it is disbursed to member's deposit account.
                                        </label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </fieldset>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card accordion-item mb-3" id="RiskMitigationDiv">
                <h2 class="accordion-header" id="headingPaymentMethod3">
                    <button type="button"
                            class="accordion-button collapsed"
                            data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                            data-bs-target="#collapsePaymentMethod3"
                            aria-expanded="false"
                            aria-controls="collapsePaymentMethod3">
                        Risk mitigation
                        <i class="mdi mdi-help-circle text-primary ms-2" data-bs-toggle="tooltip" title="Risk Mitigation: This section allows you to specify risk mitigation measures associated with the loan application. Here's an overview of the key components:
Key Points:
1. Collateral: Check this box if the borrower has provided collateral for the loan.
2. Guarantor: Check this box if the borrower has provided a guarantor for the loan.
3. Share Account Coverage Amount: Enter the amount covered by the borrower's share account, if applicable.
4. Saving Account Coverage Rate: Specify the coverage rate provided by the borrower's saving account, if applicable.
5. Salary Account Coverage Rate: Enter the coverage rate provided by the borrower's salary account, if applicable.
By carefully considering and implementing appropriate risk mitigation measures in this section, you can minimize the potential losses associated with the loan and protect the interests of the lender."></i>

                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="collapsePaymentMethod3"
                     class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                     aria-labelledby="headingPaymentMethod3"
                     data-bs-parent="#collapsibleSection">
                    <br />

                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <fieldset class="fieldset-custom">
                            <div class="row g-4">
                                <div class="col-12">
                                    <div class="form-check">
                                        @Html.CheckBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.RequiredDownPaymentCoverageRate,
                                            new { @class = "form-check-input", @id = "downPaymentCheckbox" })
                                        <label id="downpaymentrate" class="form-check-label" for="downPaymentCheckbox">Does this application require down payment?</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div class="col-12">
                                    <div class="form-check">
                                        @Html.CheckBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.IsThereGuarantor, new { @class = "form-check-input" })
                                        <label class="form-check-label" for="isActive">Has the member provided a guarantor or co-obligator ?</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="col-12">
                                    <div class="form-check">
                                        @Html.CheckBoxFor(m => m.AddLoanApplicationCommand.IsThereCollateral, new { @class = "form-check-input" })
                                        <label class="form-check-label" for="isActive">Has member provided collateral?</label>
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <hr />


                                <div class="col-md-12">
                                    <div class="form-floating form-floating-outline">
